## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook **"coverage-touching" test suite** — every production method is invoked (giving you line coverage) but almost nothing is actually verified. Here's the severity-ranked breakdown:

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Assertion-Free Tests (Fire-and-Forget)

| # | Test | Problem |
|---|------|---------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` | Zero assertions. Proves only that `Save` doesn't throw. |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` | Calls `UpdatePrice` but never verifies the price changed. A bug where the old price is re-saved would pass. |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` | Never asserts the product is gone. `Delete` could be a no-op. |
| 4 | `GetProductCount_Works` | Captures the count but never asserts it. Always passes. |
| 5 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | Applies 10% off but never checks any resulting price. The formula `Price * (1 - fraction)` could be wrong and this test would still pass. |
| 6 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` | Imports data but never checks it was stored or parsed correctly. |

**Fix pattern:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_UpdatesStoredPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
}
```

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Shallow / Trivial Assertions

| # | Test | Problem |
|---|------|---------|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` | Asserts `IsNotNull` only — never checks SKU, Name, or Price. A method returning `new Product("","",0)` would pass. |
| 8 | `SearchProducts_Works` | Asserts results `IsNotNull` — never checks count or content. A query for "Widget" returning "Gadget" passes fine. |
| 9 | `GetAllProducts_Works` | Same: `IsNotNull` on the list, no count or content check. |
| 10 | `ExportToCsv_Works` | Asserts CSV `IsNotNull` — an empty string passes. |

**Fix pattern:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetProduct_ReturnsCorrectProduct()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    var result = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", result!.Sku);
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", result.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, result.Price);
}

[TestMethod]
public void Search_ReturnsOnlyMatchingProducts()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
    var results = _catalog.Search("Widget");
    Assert.AreEqual(1, results.Count);
